{"name":"Run Lola Run","hex":"#da2811","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"run","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Kirundi."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move swiftly.\n To move forward quickly upon two feet by alternately making a short jump off either foot.","To move forward quickly upon two feet by alternately making a short jump off either foot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/run"},{"term":"lola","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a grandmother"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Run Lola Run","blocks":[{"text":"Run Lola Run is a 1998 German avant-garde thriller film written and directed by Tom Tykwer. It follows a woman named Lola who needs to obtain 100,000 marks in 20 minutes to save the life of her boyfriend, Manni."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/Lola_Rennt_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Run_Lola_Run","wikidata":"Q468697"},{"title":"Run Lola Run (soundtrack)","blocks":[{"text":"Run Lola Run (Original Motion Picture Soundtrack) is the soundtrack album to the 1998 film Run Lola Run directed by Tom Tykwer, who also co-composed the film music and score with his collaborators Johnny Klimek and Reinhold Heil. The soundtrack was released by TVT Records on 15 June 1999, featuring 16 songs mostly contributed from Franka Potente and Susie van der Meer, along with various remixes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/86/Run_Lola_Run_%28soundtrack%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Run_Lola_Run_(soundtrack)","wikidata":"Q136106179"},{"title":"Lola (given name)","blocks":[{"text":"Lola is a feminine given name and nickname in the Romance languages, and other language groups."}],"image":"https: